  "query_preview": ".. After showers wrap up later today, pattern through\nthe middle of next week will be characterized by mostly dry\nweather and near to slightly below normal temperatures as upper\nflow flattens out and high pressure builds. Only exception will be\n30 to 50% chance of light rain north of Hwy 29 Saturday evening as\ntransient shortwave and weak cold front move through the upper \nMidwest. Otherwise, frost/freeze setup remains on track for Friday\nnight into Saturday morning, and again Sunday night into Monday \nmorning as surface high sits overhead and 850 mb temperatures fall\nto near, or even slightly below, 0C. As it stands now, better \nsetup for a widespread frost/freeze event looks to be early Monday\nmorning. With mostly clear skies providing effective radiational \ncooling, some of the cold spots across the north may even dip \nbelow freezing during this time. Will continue to monitor for \nheadline potential.",
